00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:54,300
But first, let's back up.

188
00:07:54,300 --> 00:07:57,380
It's very important to remember the difference in logic

189
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:00,220
between necessary and sufficient conditions.

190
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,340
Necessary and sufficient conditions.

191
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:07,100
So if something's a necessary condition,

192
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:09,020
this means that if you don't have it,

193
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:09,780
you don't have it.

194
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:11,820
If you lack a necessary condition for x,

195
00:08:11,820 --> 00:08:14,260
you definitely don't have x.

196
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:15,940
On the other hand, sufficient conditions

197
00:08:15,940 --> 00:08:19,460
tell you if you've got the stuff, you've got x.

198
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:21,620
But there could be lots of other ways of doing it.

199
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:23,180
So if you lack a necessary condition,

200
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,900
then you don't have the thing you want.

201
00:08:24,900 --> 00:08:27,900
If you lack a sufficient condition, you might still have it.

202
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,900
Because there could be many different sufficient

203
00:08:29,900 --> 00:08:30,940
conditions.

204
00:08:30,940 --> 00:08:32,740
So you think about this.

205
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:36,700
So suppose someone has been, yeah,

